    "created_at": "2016-05-14T19:18:28Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-17T09:44:38Z",
    "body": "Notes:\n- `<legend align=left/right>` in vertical works in WebKit/Chromium but not in Gecko/Edge. I've specified WebKit/Chromium behavior.\n  \n  ```\n  <!DOCTYPE html>\n  <style>html { writing-mode: vertical-lr } </style>\n  <fieldset><legend align=left>left</legend><p align=left>left p</fieldset>\n  <fieldset><legend align=center>center</legend><p align=center>center p</fieldset>\n  <fieldset><legend align=right>right</legend><p align=right>right p</fieldset>\n  ```\n  \n  http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/4196\n  \n  Bugs:\n  https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1273433\n  https://developer.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-edge/platform/issues/7583968/\n- A `form` in quirks mode has a block-end margin in Gecko/Edge; bottom margin in WebKit/Chromium. I've specified Gecko/Edge behavior.\n  \n  ```\n  <style>html { writing-mode: vertical-lr } </style>\n  x<form id=form></form>y\n  <script>\n  w('marginRight ' + getComputedStyle(form).marginRight);\n  w('marginBottom ' + getComputedStyle(form).marginBottom);\n  </script>\n  ```\n  \n  http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/4197\n  \n  Bugs:\n  https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=157788\n  https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=612424\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
